<title>USA: Enron, Portland seek to pass hurdles.</title>
<headline>Enron, Portland seek to pass hurdles.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A commitment by Enron Corp and Portland General Electric to develop renewable resources and keep tabs on power prices will boost chances of their merger being approved in Oregon, but the deal still faces hurdles, industry sources said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The two companies reached the agreement with 13 environmental and consumer groups in exchange for endorsement of their merger.</p>
<p>Several of the newly-amenable groups, such as Oregon Energy Coordinators Association and Community Action Directors of Oregon, had previously protested the merger plans.</p>
